# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  Fonts - the important one
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Only a font whose licence allows redistribution may be committed. Inter is
# under the SIL Open Font License and ships with the app, its licence beside it
# in fonts/LICENSE-Inter.txt. Everything else in fonts/ stays out - above all
# Apple's SF Pro, whose licence covers designing for Apple platforms and does
# not permit redistribution. fonts/README.txt explains, and is deliberately NOT
# ignored.
fonts/*.otf
fonts/*.ttf
fonts/*.ttc
fonts/*.woff
fonts/*.woff2
!fonts/InterVariable.ttf
!fonts/InterVariable-Italic.ttf

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#  Local, generated, or machine-specific
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
_selftest/
_run.log
*.log

# Shortcuts hold absolute paths to one machine's folders.
*.lnk

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ...but vendor/ ships real native extension modules, and .pyd is caught by the
# [cod] above. Without this exception the repository contained the Python half
# of the WinRT projection and none of the binaries, so every clone failed with
# "No module named 'winrt'" - the precise bug vendor/ exists to prevent.
!vendor/**/*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Anything that looks like a credential or a private config. Belt and braces:
# nothing here writes these, but a stray copy must not be publishable.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
settings.local.json

# Editor / OS litter
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Agent status bus (runtime state, mirrored from %APPDATA%)
.agentbus/
_media.log

# Local render previews
_preview/

# Mirrored layout + widget diagnostics (runtime state)
.boardstate/
_widgets.log
